in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*$0\\cdot 0=0$* \n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =(0+1)\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A7}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{addition of integers}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A5}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A3}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A5}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =(0+1)\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A7}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =1\\cdot 0 &  & [\\,\\text{addition of integers}\\,] \\\\ 0\\cdot 0 & =0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A5}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "0e561cf1-bbce-5b45-99d8-35b7ea403736"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423673 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423671 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c610fab-a6ec-5612-9143-78410e0c0685" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "addition of matrices in $T$ is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423660} {:answer/id #uuid "952805ec-db79-5003-ab44-c608da27648b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "there exists a matrix $A\\in T$ such that $A+B\\ne O$ for any $B\\in T.$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423662} {:answer/id #uuid "97a1f3dc-dc3c-53f9-b457-30bca1c9f80b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$T$ does not contain the zero matrix $O$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423663} {:answer/id #uuid "d008fb5f-392d-5a1e-8353-f48e8e0933c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "addition of matrices in $T$ is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423665} {:answer/id #uuid "f89006ab-36a7-5769-850c-8ee5d58a71d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplication by a scalar is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423667}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423667} :answer-field/id #uuid "047ee837-df71-5e5c-bcee-335a715a816d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "87c89c45-3edb-5cd5-88f1-a3ee2b4d8003" :question/math-academy-id "q-35640" :question/problem "Let $T$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices $({a}_{ij})$  with real entries, such that  ${a}_{11}+{a}_{22}$ is rational.  Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$T$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to addition of matrices and multiplication of matrices by a real number) because $\\text{____}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is \n\n*$T$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to addition of matrices and multiplication of matrices by a real number) because **multiplication by a scalar is not closed.** *\n\n For example, the identity matrix \n\n$$\nI=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nlies in $T$, but\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{2}\\cdot I=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\notin T\n$$\n\nbecause $\\sqrt{2}+\\sqrt{2}$ is not a rational number.\n\nOn the other hand,\n\n- The zero matrix belongs to $T.$  $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of matrices with real entries is commutative, in general.    $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of matrices with real entries is associative, in general.    $\\,✓$\n\n- Given any $A\\in T,$  the additive inverse matrix $-A=(-1)\\cdot A$ is also in  $T,$ and   $A+(-A)=O.$  $\\,✓$"} :step/id #uuid "467837ce-9aea-5bd2-99a0-3354bf395104" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423675}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423674 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423670 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f2283d3-68c5-5fca-946c-408c6fb2b791" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423658} {:answer/id #uuid "506393e5-9110-55a4-ad28-86b41af5f7b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423659} {:answer/id #uuid "94a3dcc7-829d-5b5b-838b-243af61af1c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423661} {:answer/id #uuid "b61ef8ae-4ec6-5626-8687-752c08d8c0f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\text{A2}$, $\\text{A4}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423664} {:answer/id #uuid "f44ae4d3-7509-5333-9443-9a689afb980d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$\\text{A1}$, $\\text{A3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423666}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423659} :answer-field/id #uuid "29e9d841-9401-5444-9a3a-2b082af4b7ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186423669}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "2d091317-3092-5633-8a6e-4652d2fd3389" :question/math-academy-id "q-106941" :question/problem "From top to bottom, fill in the blanks and hence complete the proof of the following statement using the axioms $[\\text{A}1]-[\\text{A}8]$ given below.\n\n*Statement: *\n\n*If $u$ and $v$ are vectors such that $x+u=x+v$ for some $x\\in V,$ then $u=v.$*\n\n*Proof:*\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+u & =x+v &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+u)+(-x) & =(x+v)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (u+x)+(-x) & =(v+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ u+(x+(-x)) & =v+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom __}\\,\\,] \\\\ u+0 & =v+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ u & =v &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe axioms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{[A1]}:x+y=y+x & \\text{[A5]}:1\\cdot x=x \\\\ \\text{[A2]}:(x+y)+z=x+(y+z) & \\text{[A6]}:\\alpha (\\beta x)=(\\alpha \\beta )x \\\\ \\text{[A3]}:x+0=x & \\text{[A7]}:(\\alpha +\\beta )x=\\alpha x+\\beta x \\\\ \\text{[A4]}:x+(-x)=0 & \\text{[A8]}:\\alpha (x+y)=\\alpha x+\\alpha y\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Using the vector space axioms, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+u & =x+v &  & [\\,\\text{given}\\,] \\\\ (x+u)+(-x) & =(x+v)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{add }-x\\text{ to both sides}\\,] \\\\ (u+x)+(-x) & =(v+x)+(-x) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A1}\\,] \\\\ u+(x+(-x)) & =v+(x+(-x)) &  & [\\,\\text{axiom }\\text{A2}\\,] \\\\ u+0 & =v+0 &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A4}\\,] \\\\ u & =v &  & [\\,\\text{axiom A3}\\,]\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "bbaac633-758e-54a8-bb41-3769e90b4fe8" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423672}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423675 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419007 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "313cdc82-5d69-5af4-95bb-ace914a012ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "multiplication of $f\\in A$ by a scalar is not closed" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418996} {:answer/id #uuid "4f43eb35-6698-556b-937a-7540b2eaa194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "addition of functions in $A$  is not associative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418997} {:answer/id #uuid "54d7d70f-b06b-5dba-8920-ce4be2335648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "addition of functions in $A$  is not commutative" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418999} {:answer/id #uuid "61ff392f-4de3-5c34-9123-789573d772b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "$1\\cdot f\\ne f$ for some $f\\in A$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419000} {:answer/id #uuid "f187a6fa-78fb-565f-9a52-c1915abb65f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499} :answer/value "addition and scalar multiplication of functions  in $A$ do not satisfy the distributive laws" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419005}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418996} :answer-field/id #uuid "4628fceb-08d9-5ba5-86ad-00d444e18706" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419006}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "1a47334c-0a05-5b9c-b7eb-76cf4c1d5cfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-94792" :question/problem "Let $A$ be the set of all functions $f:R\\to R$ of the form  $f(x)=a+{x}^{2},$ where $a\\in R.$ Complete the following sentence:\n\n*$A$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication) because $\\text{_________}\\,.$*" :question/worked-solution "The correct answer is as follows:\n\n*$A$ is **not** a vector space (with respect to function addition and scalar multiplication) because **multiplication of $f\\in A$ by a scalar is not closed.** *\n\nFor example, if $\\alpha =2$ and $f(x)={x}^{2},$ then $\\alpha f(x)=2{x}^{2}.$ So, $\\alpha f(x)\\notin A$ because the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ is not $1.$\n\nOn the other hand:\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is associative. $\\,✓$\n\n- Addition and scalar multiplication of polynomials satisfy the distributive laws.\n$\\,✓$\n\n- Addition of real valued functions  is commutative. $\\,✓$\n\n- $1\\cdot f=f$ for all $f\\in A.$ $\\,✓$"} :step/id #uuid "f72bd130-061d-5d95-9582-1d1554fa5cad" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423676}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186423676 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186396599 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b0fcd6